        <body>
            <div xml:id="d372">

                <pb facs="0630" n="1590" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1590"/>

                <head>No. 1085.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Straus to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-05-26"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 26, 1888</date>.
                        (Received June 9.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 85.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch, No. 80, of the
                    19th instant (subject: Restrictions against foreign Jews resorting to
                    Palestine), I have the honor to inclose for your information a copy of the note
                    sent by the British embassy, as well as a copy and translation of the note sent
                    by the French embassy to the Sublime Porte upon this subject, bearing date,
                    respectively, the 24th and 23d May, 1888.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">O. S. Straus.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d372-a1.xml" xpointer="d372-a1"/>
